I found a cleaner construction that stays much closer to the paper and improves the adversarial story. Rather than generic random decoys, every decoy will itself be a transformed direct product of the paper’s second \(K_4\) type, while the planted witness is a transformed direct product of its XOR-zero first type. Thus plants and decoys have the same individual marginals and the same six prescribed distances; only the paper’s XOR invariant separates them.
