codex
One final design refinement strengthens the Track B gap without lengthening the answer: replacing the modular-sum aggregate with a one-bit rotation relation reduces the compact route to one XOR pass plus one lookup pass. That permits 140 labels at `easy` while staying below 300 operations, expands the honest candidate space to over 15 million, and raises the reference pair search to roughly ten thousand comparisons. I’m applying this before freezing the local report.
